,{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KComponents"}],"type":"topic","title":"KComponents","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"KComponents"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The k-components of an undirected graph (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k ≥ 1,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the maximal sets of vertices whose induced subgraph is k-vertex-connected, that is, has more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than k vertices and stays connected after removing any k − 1 of them. The 1-components are the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connected components with an edge, the 2-components the blocks of three or more vertices; every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"k-component lies inside a (k − 1)-component. Components at one level may share fewer than k","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/KComponents"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/KComponents/maximumK":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/kcomponents\/maximumk","title":"maximumK","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The greatest k with a k-component, or 0 when no edge joins two distinct vertices."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/KComponents\/maximumK","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximumK","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}}}